// Flat merge of the salam/token port (see salam/PORTING.md "Layout — FLAT"):
// token.c + token_xml.c — one package `token`, one file.
//
// C differences:
// - token_kind_t / token_value_kind_t are `type ... = int` aliases plus
//   TK_* / TV_* constants instead of `enum`s. Two reasons:
//   (a) the current C backend miscompiles enums declared in a non-main
//       package (typedef is emitted unprefixed, uses are prefixed), and
//   (b) enum members are not reachable across packages
//       (`tok.TokenKind.Eof` is rejected), while `tok.TK_EOF` works.
//   Values are identical to the C enums, so XML dumps and `as int`
//   comparisons match the C compiler exactly.
// - token_value_t's union is a kind tag + separate typed fields
//   (ival/fval/sval/bval). TV_CHAR payloads live in ival (the codepoint),
//   as in C. The C `slen` field is dropped: a Salam `str` knows its length.
// - token_t.span (src_span_t from core/span.h) is inlined as begin_*/end_*/
//   length fields (u32, mirroring src_pos_t/src_span_t).
// - token_stream_t is arena-backed in C; here it owns a Vector<Token> —
//   call StreamFree() when done.
package token

import x "xml.salam"
import co "sal_core.salam"

// ===== token.c =====
// token_kind_t — order and values MUST stay identical to the C enum.
